From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Pablo Lassala <jpablolassala@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] main: Export the main menu and the run dialog on D-Bus under
 Caminito

Marco asks the panel for its main menu and its run dialog, which Alt+F1 and
Alt+F2 are bound to, with a _MATE_PANEL_ACTION client message on the root
window. A Wayland compositor has no such message, so there the two keys did
nothing.

Caminito, the Wayland compositor, binds the same keys and calls MainMenu and
RunDialog of org.mate.Panel at /org/mate/Panel on the session bus, each with
the key event's time. Own that name when MATE_WM_NAME is Caminito, and have
both methods do what the client message does: drop the menu from the menu
bar, else from the menu button, else open it at the pointer. What the two
actions do moves to panel-action.c for that, since panel-action-protocol.c
is only built with X11.

No event comes with a call, so a menu opened at the pointer is placed in the
panel's window the pointer is in. On Wayland the panel doesn't know where the
pointer is outside its own windows, and the menu drops from the first panel.

With any other MATE_WM_NAME, which is Marco and any other compositor, the
name isn't owned and nothing changes.
